Description: antinomie: debugger phase 3 wire contract
Author: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Origin: project
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-20

New control opcodes and fields for following forks and execs, non-stop threads and re-adopting sessions (all additive; the contract stays at revision 17):  CONFIG (0x108e) sets session options (FORK, EXEC, NONSTOP). EVENTS (0x108f) reads an all-stop session's event or a non-stop session's queue of events, with the child, parent and exec-path details of the rare kinds. THREAD_CTL (0x1090) stops, continues or steps one thread of a non-stop session. SESSIONS (0x1091) lists the live sessions and BP_LIST (0x1092) a session's breakpoints, which is how a debugger that lost its sessions across a reconnect or a restored snapshot finds them again; ATTACH flag ADOPT takes one over with a new nonce.  The second capability word (CAPS with CAPS_EXT) is only sent to a host that asks: an earlier host rejects unknown capability bits, so it keeps getting the phase 2 reply. The tail of STATUS (options, flags, parent session) and the flags of a thread entry are zero for any session an earlier host could have made. New event kinds FORK, VFORK, VFORK_DONE and CHILD appear only in sessions with options.

